{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDiracOperatorExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDiracOperatorExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QDifferentialGeometry","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalDirac.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalDirac.exists","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-exists.lean#L31-L62","doc":"**Existence of the categorical Dirac operator.**\n\nIn an `R`-linear monoidal category `C`, for any connection `∇`, any\nendomorphism representatives `nablaEndo` (`∇`) and `reeb` (`ι_ξ∇`), and\nany unit substrate parameter `q` (`q · qinv = 1`), there exists a\n`CategoricalDiracOperator R C fh` whose Dirac morphism is exactly the\n`R`-linear combination `q⁻¹ ∇ + (1 - q⁻¹) ι_ξ∇`.\n\nThis replaces the earlier `Nonempty (CategoricalDiracOperator C fh)`\nproved by a trivial identity witness: the existential now pins the\n`dirac` field to the defining formula, so the witness genuinely realises\n[`def:categorical-dirac-operator`]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-dirac-operator-exists","label":"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}